{"table":"evidence","ref":"sha256:c941bb8e2efcb2c545fdebbfec6f904193275455192bec48bcb452c5b8ab7f97/evidence/support_optimality_warrant_20261024","record":{"id":"support_optimality_warrant_20261024","kind":"semantic_review","status":"not_run","command":[],"tool":"Ordinary derivation and primary-source reading; independent semantic acceptance not run","source_ids":["chl2018_zero_temperature","chen2026_full_support","support_tex_variation","support_tex_main","support_tex_regularity"],"subject_ids":["support.optimality_criterion","support.first_variation","support.stieltjes_measure","support.moment_identity"],"details":"For another admissible beta with Stieltjes measure nu, first variation and weighted Fubini give 2D+P(gamma)[beta-gamma]=integral G dnu-integral G dmu. The bound 0<=q<=1 gives |G(s)|<=1-s; integral (1-s)dmu=integral gamma<infinity, and similarly for nu. Nonnegativity and vanishing on support make the difference nonnegative. Convexity follows by fixing a common admissible control in the control formula, using convexity of the terminal absolute value and linearity of both penalties, then taking the supremum. CHL Proposition 4 identifies this chord criterion with minimality. Conversely, atom addition and compact mass removal prove contact. No support.contact prerequisite is used, since that conditional node would import minimality into the iff. Primary PDF passages and the current long §3.5 were inspected; no formal replay or independent acceptance is asserted."},"usage":{"record_ref":"sha256:c941bb8e2efcb2c545fdebbfec6f904193275455192bec48bcb452c5b8ab7f97/evidence/support_optimality_warrant_20261024","paper_focus":[],"paper_memberships":[{"stage":"long","subgraph_ref":"sha256:7588abc48d1c21bb64c366849eaa851938d6acc6b17cf16f89ccf8b87ca26853/papers/long.json/support/0.3.1/69473417dc487cafa5e2e39b3168d2c4a8bffdad2e91b6e486de48f122dda071","roles":["associated_record"]},{"stage":"short","subgraph_ref":"sha256:b3fb22a55f09aba18f53cd9bbac859142355ee389bba5aa7bf98d